  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Sulphur&nbsp; have puckered&nbsp; S<sub>8 </sub>&nbsp;rings with crown conformation, and S<sub>6</sub> &nbsp;rings arranged in a chair conformation.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/p-block-elements-25-638sfajasd.jpg\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 192px;\" /><br />1) S-S-S bond angles in <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>8</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>6</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> rings are different<br /><br />2) Rhombic &amp; monoclinic are <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>8</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> molecules but the arrangement of the molecules in space are different.<br /><br />3)<math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>S</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> &amp; <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>O</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> both are paramagnetic according to MOT",
